  "files": [
    {
      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <math.h>\n#include <omp.h>\n\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\n\n/*\n * Compute the gravitational impact among all pairs of bodies in \n * the system.\n */\nvoid body_force(float *restrict px, float *restrict py, float *restrict pz,\n                float *restrict vx, float *restrict vy, float *restrict vz,\n                int n) {\n  #pragma omp parallel for schedule(dynamic,16)\n  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n    float fx = 0.0f;\n    float fy = 0.0f;\n    float fz = 0.0f;\n\n    #pragma omp simd reduction(+:fx,fy,fz) aligned(px,py,pz:32)\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n      float dx = px[j] - px[i];\n      float dy = py[j] - py[i];\n      float dz = pz[j] - pz[i];\n      float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\n      float inv_dist = 1.0f / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\n      float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\n\n      fx += dx * inv_dist3;\n      fy += dy * inv_dist3;\n      fz += dz * inv_dist3;\n    }\n\n    vx[i] += DT*fx;\n    vy[i] += DT*fy;\n    vz[i] += DT*fz;\n  }\n}\n\n/*\n * Read a binary dataset with initialized bodies.\n */\nvoid read_dataset(int *nbodies, float **px, float **py, float **pz,\n                  float **vx, float **vy, float **vz) {\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading nbodie value\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n\n  size_t n = *nbodies;\n  float *tmp = (float *)malloc(n * 6 * sizeof(float));\n  if (!tmp) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError allocating temporary buffer\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n\n  b = fread(tmp, n * 6 * sizeof(float), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading input values\\n\");\n    free(tmp);\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n\n  // Allocate aligned arrays for SIMD friendliness\n  posix_memalign((void**)px, 32, n * sizeof(float));\n  posix_memalign((void**)py, 32, n * sizeof(float));\n  posix_memalign((void**)pz, 32, n * sizeof(float));\n  posix_memalign((void**)vx, 32, n * sizeof(float));\n  posix_memalign((void**)vy, 32, n * sizeof(float));\n  posix_memalign((void**)vz, 32, n * sizeof(float));\n\n  for (size_t i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n    (*px)[i] = tmp[i*6 + 0];\n    (*py)[i] = tmp[i*6 + 1];\n    (*pz)[i] = tmp[i*6 + 2];\n    (*vx)[i] = tmp[i*6 + 3];\n    (*vy)[i] = tmp[i*6 + 4];\n    (*vz)[i] = tmp[i*6 + 5];\n  }\n\n  free(tmp);\n}\n\n/*\n * Write simulation results into a binary dataset.\n */\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, float *px, float *py, float *pz,\n                   float *vx, float *vy, float *vz) {\n  size_t n = (size_t)nbodies;\n  float *tmp = (float *)malloc(n * 6 * sizeof(float));\n  if (!tmp) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError allocating temporary buffer\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n\n  for (size_t i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n    tmp[i*6 + 0] = px[i];\n    tmp[i*6 + 1] = py[i];\n    tmp[i*6 + 2] = pz[i];\n    tmp[i*6 + 3] = vx[i];\n    tmp[i*6 + 4] = vy[i];\n    tmp[i*6 + 5] = vz[i];\n  }\n\n  int b = fwrite(tmp, n * 6 * sizeof(float), 1, stdout);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError writing to output\\n\");\n    free(tmp);\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n\n  free(tmp);\n}\n\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\n  int nbodies;\n  float *px, *py, *pz, *vx, *vy, *vz;\n\n  read_dataset(&nbodies, &px, &py, &pz, &vx, &vy, &vz);\n\n  /*\n   * At each simulation iteration, interbody forces are computed,\n   * and bodies' positions are integrated.\n   */\n  for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; ++iter) {\n    body_force(px, py, pz, vx, vy, vz, nbodies);\n\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(dynamic,16)\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n      px[i] += vx[i] * DT;\n      py[i] += vy[i] * DT;\n      pz[i] += vz[i] * DT;\n    }\n  }\n\n  write_dataset(nbodies, px, py, pz, vx, vy, vz);\n\n  free(px); free(py); free(pz);\n  free(vx); free(vy); free(vz);\n\n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/nbody.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Integrating SoA layout with aligned allocation, restrict qualifiers, SIMD reduction on the inner force loop (from B), and dynamic scheduling (chunk 16) for both outer loops (force computation and position update, from C) will combine memory locality, vectorization, thread-level parallelism, and load balancing to achieve further speedup beyond any individual transformation.",
  "notes": "Combined all three source transformations: A's parallel directives, B's SoA/restrict/SIMD/aligned allocation, and C's dynamic scheduling. The schedule(dynamic,16) is retained from Source C; the SIMD reduction pragma with aligned clause comes from Source B; the I/O functions are adapted to SoA as in Source B.",
